<title>USA: Puget Sound Q1 net falls after charges.</title>
<headline>Puget Sound Q1 net falls after charges.</headline>
<dateline>BELLEVUE, Wash. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands, except per-share amounts)</p>
<p>				   3 months		12 months</p>
<p>			ended 3/31	(1,2) ended 3/31	 (2)</p>
<p>				1997	 1996	1997	 1996</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>   revenues	     463,319   487,084  1,646,095  1,591,056</p>
<p> Operating income	56,828    94,346    253,077    268,061</p>
<p>Income from continuing</p>
<p>   operations	    32,608    66,616    139,844    130,240</p>
<p>Discontinued operations,</p>
<p>  net of taxes	  (2,622)     (419)    (3,769)   (27,214)</p>
<p> Net income		29,986    66,197    136,075    103,026</p>
<p>Common shares</p>
<p>   outstanding	   84,454    84,401     84,499     84,323</p>
<p>Earnings per</p>
<p>  common share (EPS):    0.29	0.72	 1.35	 0.96</p>
<p>EPS from continuing</p>
<p>  operations		 0.32	0.72	 1.39	 1.28</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said Q1 1997 results reflect its merger with Washington Energy Co in February 1997.</p>
<p>The company said Q1 1997 includes an after-tax charge of $36.3 million, or $0.43 per share, for merger costs.</p>
<p>Q1 1997 net income includes an after-tax charge of $2.6 million, $0.03 per share, to write off the its remaining investment in Washington Energy's undeveloped coal reserves and related activities in southeastern Montana, it said.</p>
<p>Puget said, excluding the charges, continuing operations for Q1 1997 would be $0.75 per share compared to $0.72 per share for same period last year.</p>
<p>Current quarter earnings include an after-tax charge of $7.5 million for the change in funding of the Residential Exchange Credit, a fund which gives utility customers a share of profits, the company said.</p>
<p>Full name is Puget Sound Energy.</p>
</text>
